PLACEHOLDER — this is NOT a real config file.

The build requires a real `app/google-services.json` from YOUR OWN Firebase
project. It is intentionally not included in this repo (see .gitignore) and must
not be invented — it contains a project-specific API key, app id, and sender id
that only Firebase can issue.

How to get it:

  1. Go to https://console.firebase.google.com and create (or open) a project.
  2. Add an Android app with package name:  com.example.notificationservicetodo
     (this must match `applicationId` / `namespace` in app/build.gradle.kts).
  3. Download the generated google-services.json.
  4. Place it at:  app/google-services.json   (next to this file).
  5. Delete this placeholder if you like — it is ignored by the build.

Without a valid google-services.json the Gradle build will fail at the
google-services plugin step.
